-fit shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap" href="/BradSmi/status/2069758122697404521">Jun 24</a></span></div><div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 whitespace-nowrap"><button class="gap-1 inline-flex items-center border border-solid font-bold has-[svg:only-child]:px-0 transition disabled:pointer-events-none focus-visible:outline disabled:opacity-50 justify-center bg-background rounded-full text-text h-8 min-w-8 px-4 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-[1.125rem] text-subtext1 hover:bg-mix-current hover:bg-mix-amount-10 active:bg-mix-current active:bg-mix-amount-15 focus-visible:bg-mix-current focus-visible:bg-mix-amount-10 outline-current -my-2 size-8 min-w-8 shrink-0 border-transparent bg-transparent p-0 text-gray-700 hover:bg-blue-500/10 hover:text-blue-500 focus-visible:outline-blue-500" aria-label="More" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" data-icon="icon-more" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="1em" height="1em" display="flex" role="img" class="size-[18px]"><path d="M3 12c0-1.1.9-2 2-2s2 .9 2 2-.9 2-2 2-2-.9-2-2zm9 2c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2s-.9-2-2-2-2 .9-2 2 .9 2 2 2zm7 0c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2s-.9-2-2-2-2 .9-2 2 .9 2 2 2z"></path></svg></button></div></div><div dir="auto" class="font-chirp max-w-full whitespace-pre-wrap break-words text-text text-body font-normal"><span class="font-chirp max-w-full whitespace-pre-wrap break-words text-inherit text-[length:inherit] font-normal">When we launched our Community-First AI Infrastructure plan in January, we made a promise: we would meet the growing demand for datacenters without straining the resources communities depend on. Water was central to that commitment.

Today we shared our progress. Since our first</span><button type="button" class="font-chirp max-w-full whitespace-pre-wrap break-words text-blue-500 text-[length:inherit] font-normal"> Show more</button></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-3 empty:hidden"><div class="relative overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-md" style="aspect-ratio:0.8;max-width:408px"><div class="relative h-full w-full"><div inert="" class="h-full w-full"><a aria-label="Infographic with a headline reading ‘Inside Microsoft’s 20-year push to cut water intensity while scaling for growth.’ A section labeled ‘By the numbers’ presents four key data points. First, a large ‘90 percent’ indicating a reduction in water use intensity since the early 2000s. Second, another ‘90 percent’ showing that Microsoft’s 2025 owned fleet runs on low- to zero-water cooling. Third, ‘2025’ noting the year Microsoft replenished more water globally than it withdrew. Fourth, ‘500 million dollars’ representing the amount invested since 2020 in more than 75 water and wastewater projects with meaningful community co-benefits. The design uses large serif typography and blue gradient backgrounds for each statistic tile." class="block h-full w-full cursor-zoom-in appearance-none border-none bg-transparent p-0 text-inherit" href="/BradSmi/status/2069758122697404521/photo/1"><img alt="Infographic with a headline reading ‘Inside Microsoft’s 20-year push to cut water intensity while scaling for growth.’ A section labeled ‘By the numbers’ presents four key data points. First, a large ‘90 percent’ indicating a reduction in water use intensity since the early 2000s. Second, another ‘90 percent’ showing that Microsoft’s 2025 owned fleet runs on low- to zero-water cooling. Third, ‘2025’ noting the year Microsoft replenished more water globally than it withdrew. Fourth, ‘500 million dollars’ representing the amount invested since 2020 in more than 75 water and wastewater projects with meaningful community co-benefits. The 